    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0496" n="1564" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">110.11 DU/2–353</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President </hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d271-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-02-03">February 3,
                        1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>:] Have had useful visit at
                    Paris. Yesterday devoted wholly to talks with top French officials largely in
                    relation to EDC.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d271-f2"/> While political difficulties
                    are great, Stassen and I feel that there is real determination on part of
                    present government, particularly Mayer and Pleven, to push this to a successful
                    conclusion. There is still a hard road ahead, but we feel that ultimate success
                    is possible and even probable.</p>
                <p>Your State of Union message was very well received and slight initial concern
                    about Formosa was quickly dissipated, so that French press this morning takes
                    sympathetic non-critical view.</p>
                <p>Today we met at SHAPE with Ridgway, Gruenther and many of your former
                        associates,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d271-f3"/> and then with Ismay, NATO
                        Council<anchor n="4" xml:id="d271-f4"/> and OEEC<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d271-f5"/> and believe we contributed to their morale and to
                    understanding of your administration’s friendly policies.</p>
                <p>[Best regards,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d271-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d271-f1-content">
                <p>This message was transmitted to the Department of State in telegram 4308 from
                    Paris, Feb. 3, with instructions that it be delivered to the President and that
                    no distribution be made except to the Acting Secretary. A memorandum by Matthews
                    attached to the source text noted that a copy of this message was delivered to
                    the White House on Feb. 3.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d271-f2" n="2" xml:id="d271-f2-content">
                <p>For a record of Dulles’ and Stassen’s meeting with French officials during the
                    morning and afternoon of Feb. 2, see telegram 4303 from Paris, Feb. 3, <ref
                        target="#pg1557">p. 1557</ref>, and telegram 4294 from London, Feb. 4, <ref
                        target="#pg1560">p. 1560</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d271-f3" n="3" xml:id="d271-f3-content">
                <p>No record of Dulles’ and Stassen’s meeting with SHAPE officers on Feb. 3 was
                    found in Department of State files.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d271-f4" n="4" xml:id="d271-f4-content">
                <p>For a record of their meeting with Lord Ismay and their attendance at the North
                    Atlantic Council meeting of Feb. 3, see telegram Polto 1325 from Paris, Feb. 3,
                        <ref target="#pg1561">p. 1561</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d271-f5" n="5" xml:id="d271-f5-content">
                <p>For a record of their meeting with the OEEC delegates, see telegram Repto 2395
                    from Paris, Feb. 4, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
